\[x^2 + 9x^4 + 6fx^2 + f^2 = 9x^4 + 6dx^2 + d^2.\]Matching coefficients, we get
\begin{align*}
1 + 6f &= 6d, \\
f^2 &= d^2.
\end{align*}From the first equation, $d - f = \frac{1}{6}.$  Since $f^2 = d^2,$ $f = d$ or $f = -d.$  We cannot have $f = d,$ so $f = -d.$  Then $-2f = \frac{1}{6},$ so $f = -\frac{1}{12}.$

